### =============================================
### ADVANCED WORKFLOW CHAOS SCENARIOS DEMO
### =============================================
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates advanced workflow-specific failure patterns
### SCENARIOS: External Event Starvation, Child Workflow Zombies, Activity Limbo, Transaction Failures
### FOCUS: Workflow debugging, manual intervention, recovery procedures
### AUDIENCE: Perfect for demonstrating complex distributed system failures
### DURATION: Allow 15-20 minutes for full comprehensive demonstration
### =============================================

### =============================================
### PHASE 1: BASELINE ADVANCED FAILURE ASSESSMENT
### =============================================

### 1. Check advanced failure states (should be empty initially)
### Expected: No active advanced failures
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/advanced-failures

### 2. Check zombie workflow states
### Expected: No zombie workflows detected
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/zombie-workflows

### 3. Check missed external events
### Expected: No missed events initially
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/missed-events

### 4. Check hanging activities by service
### Expected: No hanging activities
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/hanging-activities

### =============================================
### PHASE 2: EXTERNAL EVENT STARVATION SCENARIO
### =============================================

### 5. Create External Event Starvation Scenario
### PURPOSE: Test workflows that wait for external events that never arrive
### REAL-WORLD: Approval systems down, payment webhooks failing, API timeouts
// @name external_event_starvation_scenario
POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/scenarios
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "External Event Starvation Test",
  "description": "Simulate workflows waiting indefinitely for external events (approvals, webhooks, API responses)",
  "failure_type": "external_event_starvation",
  "target_service": "order-processor",
  "failure_rate": 0.9,
  "duration_seconds": 120,
  "enabled": true
}

### 6. Execute External Event Starvation Scenario
### EXPECTED: Creates multiple workflows waiting for events that never arrive
### MONITORING: Watch for workflows stuck waiting for approval_system, payment_gateway, etc.
@external_event_scenario_id = {{external_event_starvation_scenario.response.body.id}}

POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/scenarios/{{external_event_scenario_id}}/execute
Content-Type: application/json

### 7. Monitor missed events during starvation
### PURPOSE: See which external events are not arriving
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/missed-events

### 8. Create high-value order to trigger approval workflow during event starvation
### PURPOSE: Create a real workflow that will be affected by event starvation
POST http://localhost:3006/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": "event_starvation_test_user",
  "item": "diamond_ring",
  "total": 2500.00
}

### =============================================
### PHASE 3: CHILD WORKFLOW ZOMBIE SCENARIO
### =============================================

### 9. Create Child Workflow Zombie Scenario
### PURPOSE: Test parent workflows with child workflows that enter zombie state
### REAL-WORLD: Partial network partitions, process hangs, infinite loops in activities
// @name child_workflow_zombie_scenario
POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/scenarios
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Child Workflow Zombie State",
  "description": "Simulate child workflows that enter zombie state (running but never complete)",
  "failure_type": "child_workflow_zombie",
  "target_service": "batch-processor",
  "failure_rate": 0.8,
  "duration_seconds": 90,
  "enabled": true
}

### 10. Execute Child Workflow Zombie Scenario
### EXPECTED: Creates parent workflow with multiple zombie child workflows
### MONITORING: Parent workflow stuck waiting for children that never complete
@child_zombie_scenario_id = {{child_workflow_zombie_scenario.response.body.id}}

POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/scenarios/{{child_zombie_scenario_id}}/execute
Content-Type: application/json

### 11. Monitor zombie workflows
### PURPOSE: See which child workflows are stuck in zombie state
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/zombie-workflows

### 12. Create bulk order to trigger child workflows during zombie scenario
### PURPOSE: Create real parent-child workflow that will be affected by zombie pattern
POST http://localhost:3007/bulk-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": "zombie_workflow_test",
  "items": [
    {"item": "laptop", "quantity": 1, "price": 1200.0},
    {"item": "monitor", "quantity": 2, "price": 300.0},
    {"item": "keyboard", "quantity": 1, "price": 100.0},
    {"item": "mouse", "quantity": 1, "price": 50.0}
  ]
}

### =============================================
### PHASE 4: ACTIVITY EXECUTION LIMBO SCENARIO
### =============================================

### 13. Create Activity Execution Limbo Scenario
### PURPOSE: Test activities that start but never complete or fail
### REAL-WORLD: Long-running operations without timeouts, blocking on unavailable resources
// @name activity_limbo_scenario
POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/scenarios
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Activity Execution Limbo",
  "description": "Simulate activities that hang indefinitely, consuming resources without completion",
  "failure_type": "activity_execution_limbo",
  "target_service": "payments",
  "failure_rate": 0.7,
  "duration_seconds": 75,
  "enabled": true
}

### 14. Execute Activity Execution Limbo Scenario
### EXPECTED: Activities consume resources but never return results
### MONITORING: Resource exhaustion, workflows suspended indefinitely
@activity_limbo_scenario_id = {{activity_limbo_scenario.response.body.id}}

POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/scenarios/{{activity_limbo_scenario_id}}/execute
Content-Type: application/json

### 15. Monitor hanging activities
### PURPOSE: See which activities are stuck in limbo state
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/hanging-activities

### 16. Create orders to trigger payment activities during limbo scenario
### PURPOSE: Create workflows that will call hanging payment activities
POST http://localhost:3006/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": "activity_limbo_test_user",
  "item": "smartphone",
  "total": 800.00
}

### =============================================
### PHASE 5: DISTRIBUTED TRANSACTION FAILURE SCENARIO
### =============================================

### 17. Create Distributed Transaction Failure Scenario
### PURPOSE: Test saga pattern failures during compensation (rollback)
### REAL-WORLD: Network partitions during rollback, compensation activity failures
// @name transaction_failure_scenario
POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/scenarios
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Distributed Transaction Compensation Failure",
  "description": "Simulate failures during distributed transaction compensation/rollback operations",
  "failure_type": "distributed_transaction_failure",
  "target_service": "inventory",
  "failure_rate": 0.6,
  "duration_seconds": 60,
  "enabled": true
}

### 18. Execute Distributed Transaction Failure Scenario
### EXPECTED: Partial rollback state with data inconsistencies
### MONITORING: Compensation failures, manual intervention required
@transaction_failure_scenario_id = {{transaction_failure_scenario.response.body.id}}

POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/scenarios/{{transaction_failure_scenario_id}}/execute
Content-Type: application/json

### 19. Create orders that will fail during shipping to trigger compensation
### PURPOSE: Force orders through full transaction then fail during shipping
POST http://localhost:3006/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": "transaction_failure_test",
  "item": "fragile_item",
  "total": 450.00
}

### =============================================
### PHASE 6: COMPREHENSIVE MONITORING & ANALYSIS
### =============================================

### 20. Get comprehensive advanced failure state overview
### PURPOSE: See all active advanced failures across the system
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/advanced-failures

### 21. Filter external event starvation failures specifically
### PURPOSE: Focus on event starvation issues
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/advanced-failures?type=external_event_starvation

### 22. Filter child workflow zombie failures specifically
### PURPOSE: Focus on zombie workflow issues
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/advanced-failures?type=child_workflow_zombie

### 23. Get all diagnostic events for advanced scenarios (last 50)
### PURPOSE: Rich debugging data for dashboard consumption
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/events?limit=50

### 24. Get critical events specifically (likely from advanced scenarios)
### PURPOSE: High-priority events requiring immediate attention
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/events?severity=critical&limit=25

### 25. Monitor missed events by specific event source
### PURPOSE: Track which external systems are causing event starvation
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/missed-events?source=approval_system

### =============================================
### PHASE 7: RECOVERY SIMULATION & MANUAL INTERVENTION
### =============================================

### 26. Simulate recovery for external event starvation
### PURPOSE: Demonstrate manual event injection and recovery procedures
### NOTE: Replace {{external_event_scenario_id}} with actual correlation ID
POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/advanced-failures/{{external_event_scenario_id}}/recover
Content-Type: application/json

### 27. Simulate recovery for child workflow zombies
### PURPOSE: Demonstrate zombie child cleanup and parent workflow recovery
### NOTE: Replace with actual parent workflow correlation ID from zombie scenario
POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/advanced-failures/parent_workflow_{{child_zombie_scenario_id}}/recover
Content-Type: application/json

### 28. Simulate recovery for hanging activities
### PURPOSE: Demonstrate activity timeout and resource cleanup
### NOTE: Replace with actual correlation ID from limbo scenario
POST http://localhost:3010/chaos/advanced-failures/{{activity_limbo_scenario_id}}/recover
Content-Type: application/json

### 29. Check recovery status - should show reduced failure counts
### PURPOSE: Verify that recovery procedures were effective
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/advanced-failures

### 30. Verify zombie cleanup was successful
### PURPOSE: Confirm no zombie workflows remain after recovery
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/zombie-workflows

### =============================================
### PHASE 8: END-TO-END CORRELATION TRACKING
### =============================================

### 31. Get events correlated to external event starvation scenario
### PURPOSE: Complete end-to-end tracing of event starvation workflow
### NOTE: Replace {{external_event_scenario_id}} with actual correlation ID
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/events?correlation_id={{external_event_scenario_id}}&limit=100

### 32. Get events correlated to zombie workflow scenario
### PURPOSE: Complete end-to-end tracing of zombie workflow creation and resolution
### NOTE: Replace {{child_zombie_scenario_id}} with actual correlation ID
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/events?correlation_id={{child_zombie_scenario_id}}&limit=100

### 33. Final system status check
### PURPOSE: Overall system health after advanced chaos testing
GET http://localhost:3010/chaos/status

### =============================================
### ADVANCED WORKFLOW DEBUGGING DEMONSTRATION POINTS
### =============================================
###
### 🎯 KEY ADVANCED FEATURES FOR DASHBOARDS:
###
### 1. WORKFLOW STATE VISUALIZATION:
###    - Show workflows stuck in specific states (waiting, zombie, limbo)
###    - Display parent-child workflow dependency graphs
###    - Highlight workflows requiring manual intervention
###
### 2. EXTERNAL EVENT TRACKING:
###    - Monitor expected vs actual external events
###    - Track event source reliability and timeouts
###    - Show workflow approval bottlenecks and delays
###
### 3. ZOMBIE WORKFLOW DETECTION:
###    - Identify child workflows that never complete
###    - Track resource consumption by zombie processes
###    - Display parent workflows waiting indefinitely
###
### 4. ACTIVITY EXECUTION MONITORING:
###    - Show activities consuming resources without completion
###    - Track hanging activities by service and type
###    - Monitor resource exhaustion patterns
###
### 5. DISTRIBUTED TRANSACTION ANALYSIS:
###    - Visualize saga compensation failure patterns
###    - Track partial rollback states and data inconsistencies
###    - Show manual intervention requirements
###
### 6. RECOVERY PROCEDURE TRACKING:
###    - Document manual intervention actions taken
###    - Track recovery success rates and procedures
###    - Show workflow restart and cleanup operations
###
### 7. CORRELATION AND TRACING:
###    - End-to-end workflow failure correlation
###    - Cross-service failure impact analysis
###    - Timeline visualization of failure progression
###
### 8. REAL-TIME ALERTING:
###    - Critical events requiring immediate attention
###    - SLA violation alerts for hanging workflows
###    - Resource exhaustion warnings
###
### =============================================
### 🚀 ADVANCED SCENARIO DEMONSTRATION GUIDE:
###
### TIMING: Execute phases sequentially with 2-3 minute observation periods
### MONITORING: Keep notifications UI (localhost:8080) open for live updates
### ANALYSIS: Use correlation IDs for complete workflow tracing
### RECOVERY: Demonstrate manual intervention capabilities
### CLEANUP: Recovery endpoints simulate real-world intervention procedures
###
### EXPECTED DEMO DURATION: 15-20 minutes for complete advanced scenarios
### ADVANCED FAILURE TYPES: 4 distinct workflow-specific failure patterns
### NOTIFICATION RATE: Expect 15-30 critical/error events per scenario
### RECOVERY PROCEDURES: 3-5 manual intervention actions per scenario type
### =============================================

### =============================================
### 🎭 REAL-WORLD SCENARIO MAPPING:
###
### 1. EXTERNAL EVENT STARVATION → HR approval workflows, payment webhooks, API integrations
### 2. CHILD WORKFLOW ZOMBIE → Batch processing, multi-tenant operations, fan-out patterns
### 3. ACTIVITY EXECUTION LIMBO → External API calls, database operations, file processing
### 4. DISTRIBUTED TRANSACTION FAILURE → E-commerce checkouts, financial transactions, inventory management
###
### These scenarios represent the most challenging distributed system failures
### that require manual intervention and sophisticated monitoring to resolve.
### =============================================
